    "headline": "SRF Ltd dominates with exceptional profitability and integrated diversification moat",
    "reason": "SRF's outperformance is driven by diversification across specialty chemicals, fluorochemicals, and packaging films that creates pricing power and margin resilience. The company demonstrates structural cost leadership with raw material costs at only 45% versus 65-66% for peers, enabling gross margins of 54.7% (20+ percentage points above peers). This translates to EBITDA margins of 22% (double the segment median) and PAT margins of 11.6% (4-5x peers). The integrated model across chemicals and films provides backward integration benefits. Strong ROCE of 14.6% and ROE of 14.3% (double peer medians) reflect superior capital efficiency. Negative working capital days (-12 vs +12 median) indicate strong supplier terms and cash generation. The diversification strategy noted in sources provides resilience against the commodity cyclicality that plagues pure-play film manufacturers like Polyplex.",
    "india_vs_global": "SRF's profitability metrics significantly exceed even Toray Industries (Japan's integrated giant with 9.4% EBITDA margin vs SRF's 22%), demonstrating that the Indian player has built a genuinely world-class competitive position through its diversified chemicals-films integration rather than just benefiting from local market dynamics."
